\details{
A conditional check holds fitted random effects fixed. A marginal check
averages over their fitted distribution. When responses share random effects
or residual correlation, they must be simulated together to preserve that
dependence; this is called joint response simulation below. Whether responses
are independent depends on the chosen conditioning, not just the model class.
\subsection{Coverage}{

PIT means probability integral transform: the fitted cumulative distribution
function (CDF) maps each observation to a probability. At discrete values,
that probability is randomised over the corresponding probability mass.
Quantile residuals transform PIT values to standard-normal scores.
A posterior predictive check (PPC) compares observed responses with simulated
data sets that also include approximate uncertainty in fitted parameters.

This table applies to the supported response families described below.
\tabular{llllll}{
Fitter \tab PIT/quantile \tab Uniform QQ \tab Simulated QQ \tab Scalable plots \tab PPC \cr
lm/glm \tab Yes \tab Yes \tab Yes \tab Yes \tab Approximate coefficient draws \cr
mgcv::gam \tab Yes \tab Depends on family \tab Yes \tab Yes \tab Coefficients drawn together \cr
mgcv::bam \tab Marginal families \tab Marginal or joint \tab Gaussian AR1; otherwise marginal for GEE \tab Yes \tab Excludes GEE AR1 \cr
gamm/nlme::lme \tab Conditional/marginal \tab Depends on independence \tab Gaussian; PQL limits \tab Yes \tab Gaussian; approximate PQL without residual correlation \cr
gamm4/lme4::merMod \tab Conditional/marginal \tab Depends on independence \tab Joint, including GLMMs \tab Yes \tab Conditional/marginal \cr
glmmTMB \tab Conditional/marginal \tab Depends on independence \tab Joint, including non-Gaussian \tab Yes \tab Conditional/marginal \cr
GJRM::gamlss \tab Seven univariate families \tab Yes \tab Yes \tab Yes \tab Coefficients drawn together \cr
sdmTMB \tab Depends on treatment of fields \tab Depends on independence \tab Joint, including delta \tab Yes \tab Parameters and fields drawn together \cr
}
\itemize{
\item \code{lm}/\code{glm}: weighted Gaussian and supported response families, with their
fitted dispersion. Quasi families do not specify a response distribution,
so they do not support PIT/quantile residuals or PPCs.
\item \code{gam}/\code{bam}: ordinary, distributional and grouped families, including
weighted Gamma, inverse Gaussian, \code{twlss}, ordinal and \code{ziP} distributions.
Multivariate-normal PITs check each response separately; simulations retain
covariance between responses. Nominal multinomial models retain traditional
residual checks and PPCs. PITs would require an ordering of their categories.
\item \code{gamm}/\code{gamm4} and direct \code{lme}/\code{merMod} fits use their full predictors.
Gaussian nlme variance weights and residual covariance are retained.
Non-Gaussian \code{gamm} fits use penalized quasi-likelihood (PQL). Without residual
correlation, these support approximate response checks and PPCs based on
their fitted working parameters. PQL residual correlation acts on the
working response used for fitting; it does not specify a joint distribution
for the observed responses.
\item \code{glmmTMB}: conditional Gaussian, Poisson, binomial, NB1/NB2, beta, Gamma,
Tweedie, lognormal and supported truncated distributions, including fitted
zero inflation and dispersion. Marginal simulations also provide reference
samples for other families that glmmTMB can simulate. Unsupported conditional
family CDFs remain unavailable. The package's own joint simulator preserves
temporal AR1, spatial covariance and correlated random slopes.
\item Univariate \code{GJRM::gamlss}: uncensored N, LN, GA, GAi, P, NBI and NBII.
Probabilities use the final likelihood parameters. This corrects stored NBII
probabilities that use a Poisson CDF in some upstream versions. Other
families and joint, censored and survival models are not yet supported.
\item \code{sdmTMB}: supported single-response and delta families retain spatial,
spatiotemporal, grouping, time-varying and smooth effects. Standard deltas
and deltas with the coupled Poisson link support checks of the complete
response, occurrence and positive component. sdmTMB's transformations from
internal parameters to response parameters must be available.
}
